        {
          "lesson": "Verify a claims-to-reference-table join in two layers before using any joined attribute: (1) run join_check on the exact key pair to record cardinality, right_key_unique, unmatched_left and its denominator; (2) perform the merge with how=left and validate=many_to_one so the merge itself asserts the relationship and records rows_before, rows_after and unmatched. Rely on joined columns only when rows_after == rows_before and unmatched == 0; otherwise report the shortfall as an explicit filter with its denominator. (From the passing T3 plan, 4.0/4.0 with no failed checks; no evaluator feedback was issued.)",
